<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The driver's Process half's git-only classes (PROC1b, PROC1c): the Process classes that start git and
  nothing a neighbour's load could fail carry Parallel=Git beside Category=Process, and run four at once
  in one host. process.runsettings runs every other Process class, eight at once (PROCPAR1), with
  the classes that share the process run alone after the rest. The driver's
  Category.cs says which classes may carry the trait, and its CategoryTests holds them to it.

  Four, in one host: PROC1a measured the half as git starts made one at a time, four classes at once at
  about 2.2 times the throughput, and no gain from eight in one host or from a second host past four at
  once, since every start slows past about four whichever host makes it (FLAKE1's FIX-LOG entry). A class
  is xUnit's unit of parallel work, so the longest class is this run's wall.

  The name ends in process.runsettings on purpose: the merge tool reads a gate run with such a file as a
  Process half (isProcessGate), so this one too keeps its trx and re-runs a failed test alone. Its filter
  is in the file for the same reason as the other's: VSTest ANDs it with the one the re-run adds.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <TestCaseFilter>Category=Process&amp;Parallel=Git</TestCaseFilter>
  </RunConfiguration>
  <xUnit>
    <ParallelizeTestCollections>true</ParallelizeTestCollections>
    <MaxParallelThreads>4</MaxParallelThreads>
  </xUnit>
</RunSettings>
